1
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:17,520
Aiming for the setting sun
floating on the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:24,660
when I kick a pebble, even my shoes fly off.

3
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:32,920
Onto the head of the
carpenter who was snipping away,

4
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:39,140
they laughed that I was still just a kid.

5
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:44,220
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:44,220 --> 00:00:49,300
nothing changes, not even one single yawn.

7
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:53,180
The town somehow feels so gentle.

8
00:00:54,660 --> 00:01:01,140
From the pointed hat's hand-washing basin,

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:07,460
the sun sinks toward the great sky.

10
00:01:11,650 --> 00:01:15,920
Tomorrow too, it seems to end again.

11
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:21,020
Katsushika, Shibamata,
once again even happiness is lost.

12
00:01:21,020 --> 00:01:24,520
Because I'm a fool who only
realized it after hearing it.

13
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:36,300
Locker

14
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:44,080
A metal box for storing changing clothes and daily necessities,
found everywhere in offices, schools, and so on.

15
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:49,920
This is a horror story
surrounding that locker.

16
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:54,960
Aaaaaah!

17
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:09,200
Aaaaaah!

18
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:17,640
Aaaaaah! Chief, opening someone's locker
without saying a word is just terrible!

19
00:02:18,200 --> 00:02:20,860
I was planning to tidy it up later,
you know.

20
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:23,700
Please don't do unnecessary things.

21
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:24,740
Wait, stop!

22
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:27,020
How many times do I have to tell you?

23
00:02:27,020 --> 00:02:30,120
Didn't I tell you not to
bring toys into the police box?

24
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,960
Can't I have just a little bit?

25
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:34,500
They're for relaxing during break time.

26
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:37,940
Don't give me that. You're running a
business renting out games to the kids!

27
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:38,700
What did you say?

28
00:02:39,220 --> 00:02:40,040
Is that true, Ryotsu?

29
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:42,740
That's a lie, Chief!

30
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:45,360
I'm a police officer, after all!

31
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:47,900
I would never do something like that!

32
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:48,620
Ryo-san,

33
00:02:48,620 --> 00:02:50,940
lend me Final Paradise.

34
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:54,520
I'll look for it myself, Ryo-san.

35
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:56,220
Where is it?

36
00:02:56,220 --> 00:02:58,800
Found it, this one!

37
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,440
Ryo-san, lend me this one.

38
00:03:00,440 --> 00:03:01,600
Sure, one shot for 100 yen.

39
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:04,200
Bye then, Ryo-san.

40
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:05,460
Lend it to us again sometime!

41
00:03:05,460 --> 00:03:07,820
What strange kids.

42
00:03:07,820 --> 00:03:11,140
Looks like they think this is a game shop.

43
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:12,520
Hey, Chief.

44
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:17,480
Idiot!

45
00:03:17,820 --> 00:03:19,660
I'm off on patrol.

46
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:23,140
Go outside and cool your head thoroughly.

47
00:03:23,720 --> 00:03:25,740
You're on 24-hour continuous patrol.

48
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:29,000
Phew, what a fast runner that guy is.

49
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:31,820
What are you doing, Reiko?

50
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:35,980
Today's the day they said they'd
come to replace the old locker, right?

51
00:03:35,980 --> 00:03:37,300
That's right.

52
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:40,780
If it were up to me,
I'd like to get rid of the whole locker.

53
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:51,100
Who the hell can patrol
in this freezing cold?

54
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:58,880
Isn't that Mr. Ryotsu?
What on earth happened?

55
00:03:59,940 --> 00:04:02,620
You showed up at just the right time.

56
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:12,140
Senpai, why do I have to sneak around too?

57
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:14,480
Stop your whining and just get going.

58
00:04:14,480 --> 00:04:16,680
Honestly, Senpai, you're so selfish.

59
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:18,220
Excuse me!

60
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:21,200
Senpai,
there doesn't seem to be anyone here.

61
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:24,600
Phew, I feel like a new man.

62
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,440
It's the Document Gaiden!

63
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:30,440
Senpai, what happened to this?

64
00:04:30,960 --> 00:04:33,440
My treasures, the ones I stashed away,

65
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:38,400
were damn well taken out and
left outside without permission!

66
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,920
You're not planning to get rid of them,
are you?

67
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:42,260
Wow, these really bring back memories.

68
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:43,580
The Chief's back!

69
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:48,000
Crap! If he finds out we've been slacking off on patrol,
we're in for another big scolding!

70
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:55,960
Listen, that TerAya guy is sure
to tell the Chief right away.

71
00:04:56,420 --> 00:04:57,947
But...

72
00:04:57,997 --> 00:05:01,940
Where on earth should we hide...

73
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:03,240
Here!

74
00:05:07,880 --> 00:05:08,980
Why do I have to...

75
00:05:08,980 --> 00:05:11,280
If you were alone at the police box,
you'd look suspicious, wouldn't you!

76
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:14,300
Let's make some tea.

77
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:15,000
Thanks.

78
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:15,960
Terai.

79
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:17,760
It's you, Chief.

80
00:05:18,120 --> 00:05:20,900
I thought Ryo-san had come back.

81
00:05:20,900 --> 00:05:23,820
Ryotsu? No, there was nobody here.

82
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:24,520
I see.

83
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:26,820
Terai, let me introduce you.

84
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:29,520
This is an old friend of mine.

85
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:32,600
This is Yakushiji,
who's now in narcotics enforcement.

86
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:34,100
We happened to run into each other there.

87
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:34,440
Nice to meet you.

88
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:36,720
The pleasure is mine.

89
00:05:37,200 --> 00:05:38,700
Narcotics enforcement

90
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:39,760
Sounds like hard work.

91
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,100
Well, yeah.

92
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:45,220
A large-scale drug deal is going down soon.

93
00:05:45,820 --> 00:05:48,980
We're just finishing up
preparations to catch them.

94
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:52,540
Hey, hey, is it really okay
to be talking about that here?

95
00:05:52,960 --> 00:05:55,100
Quit dawdling and yapping on forever.

96
00:05:55,100 --> 00:05:56,660
Just hurry up and get out of here.

97
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:58,360
Senpai.

98
00:05:58,360 --> 00:06:00,060
Didn't I tell you not to make a sound?

99
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:03,220
Well, I need to go pee.

100
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:03,960
What?

101
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:06,520
What was that noise?

102
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:09,380
It sounded like it came
from around that locker.

103
00:06:10,580 --> 00:06:11,440
That reminds me.

104
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:14,040
Crap, did they notice us?

105
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,180
Fail.

106
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:25,500
Excuse me.

107
00:06:27,080 --> 00:06:31,320
We were told by Katsushika
station to replace the old locker.

108
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:32,800
That's right.

109
00:06:33,940 --> 00:06:35,560
So it's the locker replacement.

110
00:06:35,560 --> 00:06:37,980
Yes! We can get out of here!

111
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:38,740
Failed.

112
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:40,960
Where should we put it?

113
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:44,120
Could you bring it over
and set it down there?

114
00:06:44,540 --> 00:06:44,940
Yes.

115
00:06:46,900 --> 00:06:48,000
Heave!

116
00:06:48,400 --> 00:06:49,320
Heave-ho!

117
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:52,780
Heave, heave, heave!

118
00:06:52,780 --> 00:06:54,600
This is kind of interesting

119
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:55,980
That's strange.

120
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:58,700
Reiko-kun seems to have
tidied it up earlier, though.

121
00:06:58,700 --> 00:06:59,960
Well, whatever.

122
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:02,440
If all that's in there is junk,
like something a dog dragged together,

123
00:07:02,440 --> 00:07:03,680
just throw it all out as is.

124
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:04,900
Yes, understood.

125
00:07:09,580 --> 00:07:11,320
Senpai, it's hot!

126
00:07:12,520 --> 00:07:14,660
You crawled out right in front of the heater,
didn't you?

127
00:07:16,660 --> 00:07:17,400
Ugh!

128
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:20,860
Ugh, this is unbearable.

129
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:22,320
Senpai.

130
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:24,640
You take your clothes off too,
it's too hot to stand!

131
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:25,060
Yes.

132
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:33,145
Nakagawa-senpai,

133
00:07:33,195 --> 00:07:37,440
two naked men pressed up
against each other like this

134
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:39,200
is so sweltering...

135
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:40,100
True enough.

136
00:07:40,780 --> 00:07:42,280
I have to pee.

137
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:44,220
What happened? Did you wet yourself?

138
00:07:44,220 --> 00:07:47,960
No, it went away.
Maybe it was from sweating.

139
00:07:48,300 --> 00:07:49,120
I see.

140
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:54,420
What's that? Something's seeping out.

141
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:56,840
What on earth is in there?

142
00:07:57,380 --> 00:07:58,440
No good!

143
00:07:59,260 --> 00:07:59,940
Whoa!

144
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:01,180
Tch!

145
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:05,420
Are you alright, Ohara?

146
00:08:06,180 --> 00:08:08,820
I just got a bit hot.
I'm going to cool off with some water.

147
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:10,540
Terai, move the heater out of the way.

148
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:11,340
Y-yes.

149
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:13,100
Senpai, are you alright?

150
00:08:14,220 --> 00:08:17,800
That was close. If we'd been found here,
it would have been the end of us.

151
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:24,620
Right, let's bring the old locker over.
Ready, one, two, heave!

152
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:28,200
Okay, once we're outside,
we're in the clear.

153
00:08:28,200 --> 00:08:33,780
Heave!

154
00:08:36,680 --> 00:08:40,020
Once we're outside, we'll wait for
the right moment and make our escape.

155
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:42,860
Are you alright?

156
00:08:51,220 --> 00:08:53,320
Handle it more carefully.

157
00:08:53,320 --> 00:08:56,560
Well then, excuse us.

158
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:09,040
Right, shall we get going now?

159
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:10,200
Please hurry.

160
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:13,000
We can't stay stuck like this forever.

161
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:19,060
Damn it, the door won't open!

162
00:09:19,060 --> 00:09:20,540
Escape is impossible...

163
00:09:21,280 --> 00:09:21,640
No way...

164
00:09:24,040 --> 00:09:27,540
So we have to live in here
for the rest of our lives?

165
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:29,340
Don't be ridiculous, that can't happen.

166
00:09:29,900 --> 00:09:30,260
But...

167
00:09:30,720 --> 00:09:33,880
Calm down, Honda,
there's definitely a chance to escape.

168
00:09:34,620 --> 00:09:35,340
Senpai

169
00:09:37,340 --> 00:09:40,720
Maybe it's because I went outside and got cold,
but I need to pee again.

170
00:09:40,720 --> 00:09:45,260
Hold it in! If you wet yourself in this position,
it'll be a terrible disaster!

171
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:49,200
But I can't hold it any longer,
I'm at my limit!

172
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:52,460
It stopped.

173
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:55,200
W-what's going on?

174
00:10:03,620 --> 00:10:06,000
I feel like something's moving.

175
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:09,080
Looks like we're being moved.

176
00:10:17,440 --> 00:10:18,380
That's the sound of...

177
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:27,240
That shock deformed the locker,
and the door won't open!

178
00:10:30,060 --> 00:10:32,040
Crap! The Prestia is right there!

179
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:33,840
Help!

180
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:49,440
Oh no!

181
00:10:50,760 --> 00:10:52,340
I'm not getting crushed!

182
00:10:55,920 --> 00:10:56,180
No way!

183
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:07,540
We somehow managed to get out

184
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:12,920
Right on time.

185
00:11:23,540 --> 00:11:24,700
Who knows.

186
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:25,840
It's moving!

187
00:11:31,360 --> 00:11:31,780
What?

188
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:40,040
Senpai, we're sinking!

189
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:41,340
You'll know if you're in there!

190
00:11:41,380 --> 00:11:43,200
Senpai, senpai, senpai, senpai!

191
00:11:43,820 --> 00:11:44,640
What the hell!

192
00:11:44,780 --> 00:11:46,780
Senpai, we're spinning like a spaceship!

193
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:35,100
I almost drowned to death back there.

194
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:36,420
Pee.

195
00:12:36,420 --> 00:12:37,340
Did you wet yourself?

196
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:38,720
Y-yeah, but it's calmed down now.

197
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:41,700
What?

198
00:12:42,540 --> 00:12:42,980
Who's there?

199
00:12:43,780 --> 00:12:46,180
So there you are, you grown-up-spitting man!

200
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:47,360
Hyah!

201
00:12:47,560 --> 00:12:50,960
Hey, wait! We're not suspicious or anything!

202
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:53,200
Shut up! Monster!

203
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:56,440
Shit! I thought you were just kids,
and now you're getting cocky!

204
00:12:57,180 --> 00:12:58,580
That's enough!

205
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:00,120
Whoa!

206
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:02,920
Hey, wait! You little brats!

207
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:06,260
Yah!

208
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:06,620
Yah!

209
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:07,740
Hyah!

210
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:09,840
You guys! You guys!

211
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:11,220
Senpai!

212
00:13:15,460 --> 00:13:17,100
Take this!

213
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:28,000
I won't forgive you!

214
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:28,900
Queen!

215
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:31,980
Queen!

216
00:13:32,540 --> 00:13:33,840
Queen!

217
00:13:34,260 --> 00:13:35,380
Queen!

218
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:35,900
Queen!

219
00:13:37,780 --> 00:13:38,900
What's that?

220
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:41,120
Water's chasing a kid.

221
00:13:42,380 --> 00:13:45,680
A suspicious guy! Let's catch
him and turn him in to the police!

222
00:13:45,740 --> 00:13:46,240
Yeah!

223
00:13:46,780 --> 00:13:47,580
Queen!

224
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:51,700
What?

225
00:13:52,140 --> 00:13:52,860
Queen!

226
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:57,500
Whoa!

227
00:13:58,140 --> 00:13:59,540
What's wrong, senpai?

228
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:00,380
I don't know what's going on.

229
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:02,680
A muscle-bound rugby team

230
00:14:02,680 --> 00:14:04,000
is coming this way.

231
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:13,160
Senpai...

232
00:14:13,520 --> 00:14:14,880
Why are we running away?

233
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:15,540
You idiot!

234
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:16,860
Two Kameari cops

235
00:14:16,860 --> 00:14:18,120
actually got into a locker

236
00:14:18,120 --> 00:14:19,560
and were chasing kids?

237
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:20,720
If the public finds out...

238
00:14:20,720 --> 00:14:22,100
how are you going to explain that?

239
00:14:31,860 --> 00:14:34,860
Nnnngghh!

240
00:14:35,580 --> 00:14:36,820
Hold on tight!

241
00:14:36,820 --> 00:14:38,360
Aaaaaah!

242
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:39,240
Nnnngghh!

243
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:49,720
Senpai, let's pry it open
quickly and get out of here.

244
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:51,560
This way, this way!

245
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:54,520
I'm so hungry.

246
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:57,340
Senpai, why are you running away?

247
00:14:57,340 --> 00:15:00,260
Oh no. Out of reflex, I ended up hiding.

248
00:15:00,800 --> 00:15:01,260
Go!

249
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:02,220
Tall one, here you go.

250
00:15:02,680 --> 00:15:03,000
Thanks.

251
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:04,280
Good work.

252
00:15:05,140 --> 00:15:05,980
Uh-oh!

253
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:13,800
If we get caught like this,
the Chief will kill us!

254
00:15:15,820 --> 00:15:16,460
That's...!

255
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:20,040
It's Pretty Yuri,
the popular female pro wrestler!

256
00:15:22,620 --> 00:15:23,440
Senpai...

257
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,480
Q-quiet!

258
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:29,980
Well, this is a perfect spot.

259
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:31,540
Senpai, I'm serious!

260
00:15:31,540 --> 00:15:32,680
Keep quiet.

261
00:15:33,860 --> 00:15:36,680
Hey, move aside! It's a tractor!

262
00:15:36,680 --> 00:15:38,960
I don't want to see your naked body!

263
00:15:40,740 --> 00:15:42,060
Damn, I didn't mean to...

264
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:44,160
Oh no, it's a peeper!

265
00:15:45,860 --> 00:15:46,780
A peeper?

266
00:15:47,160 --> 00:15:47,540
Hey!

267
00:15:47,540 --> 00:15:48,640
What?

268
00:15:49,340 --> 00:15:51,120
No, there's a reason for this...

269
00:15:51,640 --> 00:15:55,140
You've got some nerve,
sneaking into our school building.

270
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:56,820
Everyone, take them down!

271
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:22,760
We were so close, though.

272
00:16:22,760 --> 00:16:25,960
Senpai, looks like we actually got away.

273
00:16:38,680 --> 00:16:40,660
We somehow got out of that.

274
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:46,400
That locker.

275
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:48,960
I hid some things inside that locker.

276
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:51,300
Haul it up!

277
00:17:04,980 --> 00:17:06,920
It's not opening easily!

278
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:09,000
Looks like it's swaying around

279
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,720
Is the dizziness back again?

280
00:17:11,460 --> 00:17:12,420
It opened!

281
00:17:12,420 --> 00:17:13,120
We did it!

282
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:20,260
It's jammed!

283
00:17:20,260 --> 00:17:24,260
It's jammed!

284
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:30,700
Why's it open out there?

285
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:31,700
Am I going to die?

286
00:17:48,140 --> 00:17:49,320
T-this guy...

287
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:54,820
For crying out loud.

288
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:59,060
We've reached the ground,
but we still can't get out?

289
00:17:59,060 --> 00:18:01,640
Keep quiet, unless you want to die.

290
00:18:01,640 --> 00:18:01,940
No.

291
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:09,260
Did you bring the cash?

292
00:18:09,800 --> 00:18:10,020
Yeah.

293
00:18:10,560 --> 00:18:11,380
Here it is.

294
00:18:13,680 --> 00:18:15,580
Is the merchandise in that locker?

295
00:18:15,580 --> 00:18:16,460
Yes.

296
00:18:16,460 --> 00:18:20,660
To throw the police off,
we hid it in that locker.

297
00:18:20,660 --> 00:18:23,460
Then let us check the merchandise.

298
00:18:23,460 --> 00:18:25,080
That's not allowed.

299
00:18:25,080 --> 00:18:28,580
First I'll count all of your money.

300
00:18:29,540 --> 00:18:30,780
Then I'll count them.

301
00:18:30,780 --> 00:18:32,040
One.

302
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:33,200
Two.

303
00:18:33,200 --> 00:18:34,820
Three.

304
00:18:34,820 --> 00:18:35,820
Four.

305
00:18:35,820 --> 00:18:37,420
Five.

306
00:18:37,420 --> 00:18:38,680
Six.

307
00:18:38,680 --> 00:18:39,820
Seven.

308
00:18:39,820 --> 00:18:41,300
Eight.

309
00:18:41,300 --> 00:18:42,260
Nine.

310
00:18:42,980 --> 00:18:43,880
No way.

311
00:18:43,880 --> 00:18:45,620
This is a drug deal!

312
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:50,000
Why are we in a place like this?
I want to go home already!

313
00:18:50,540 --> 00:18:52,580
We have to contact the police somehow.

314
00:18:54,680 --> 00:18:55,720
That's it!

315
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:11,760
141 142 143 144 145 26 47 48

316
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:18,800
Senpai,
I don't have a ¥10 coin or a phone card.

317
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:22,680
Don't worry,
this button is here for times like this.

318
00:19:24,800 --> 00:19:28,540
I think you should take your hand off the
receiver for a moment and pull the cord.

319
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:29,580
I see.

320
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:35,420
2,999 sheets, 3,000 sheets, OK.

321
00:19:35,420 --> 00:19:36,320
Indeed.

322
00:19:37,640 --> 00:19:39,880
Then please take a look at my goods too.

323
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:43,680
There isn't any.

324
00:19:44,560 --> 00:19:46,200
Boss, over there.

325
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:48,780
When did that happen?

326
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:50,940
What on earth is going on?

327
00:19:51,340 --> 00:19:53,060
That's my line!

328
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:54,520
Don't tell me this kid's
been messing with us.

329
00:19:54,520 --> 00:19:56,820
You're not up to some funny tricks, are you?

330
00:19:58,360 --> 00:19:59,780
Alright, senpai, hurry!

331
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:02,140
1 1 0

332
00:20:02,140 --> 00:20:04,880
Right... oh no.

333
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:07,280
Hey, the locker is making a phone call.

334
00:20:08,460 --> 00:20:09,180
What?!

335
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:11,440
Damn it!
-Yes, this is the Kameari police box.

336
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:41,340
You've really set up something interesting,
haven't you.

337
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:44,689
Since we didn't know either,

338
00:20:44,739 --> 00:20:48,160
as proof of that,
I'll take care of it with my own hands.

339
00:20:54,840 --> 00:20:56,760
What the hell kind of gun is that?

340
00:20:57,380 --> 00:20:59,700
Too bad, it was so close.

341
00:20:59,700 --> 00:21:02,560
You bastard,
you deliberately shot our car, didn't you?

342
00:21:02,560 --> 00:21:05,280
This time, I'll definitely take him down.

343
00:21:10,140 --> 00:21:10,860
So close.

344
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:14,480
M-my limousine... you really did it on purpose,
didn't you, you bastard?

345
00:21:14,480 --> 00:21:17,405
No, no, though the shot didn't hit Roca,

346
00:21:17,455 --> 00:21:19,240
just watch the next one.

347
00:21:38,780 --> 00:21:40,780
Honda, Honda, hang in there!

348
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,180
I need to pee.

349
00:21:42,180 --> 00:21:42,840
Hold it in!

350
00:21:43,040 --> 00:21:44,700
But it's already come out.

351
00:21:49,600 --> 00:21:50,380
How about that!

352
00:21:50,540 --> 00:21:52,200
Just like I said, I caught him.

353
00:21:52,660 --> 00:21:55,020
Tch, you've given us so much trouble.

354
00:21:55,560 --> 00:21:58,320
Before I kill you, let me see your face.

355
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:00,360
Ngh.

356
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:00,720
Ngh.

357
00:22:06,280 --> 00:22:06,920
Ngh.

358
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:07,040
Ngh.

359
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:07,320
Ngh.

360
00:22:08,660 --> 00:22:09,300
Ngh.

361
00:22:16,560 --> 00:22:17,200
Mm

362
00:22:17,200 --> 00:22:17,220
Hmm

363
00:22:17,220 --> 00:22:17,260
Ngh

364
00:22:17,260 --> 00:22:17,720
Ugh

365
00:22:17,720 --> 00:22:17,740
Nngh

366
00:22:17,740 --> 00:22:17,760
Mm

367
00:22:21,540 --> 00:22:21,860
Ngh

368
00:22:23,760 --> 00:22:24,560
Get out of the way and look

369
00:22:25,280 --> 00:22:27,600
Honda, what? Did he pass out?

370
00:22:32,840 --> 00:22:34,760
Don't move! Police!

371
00:22:39,780 --> 00:22:40,580
Kamikata

372
00:22:40,580 --> 00:22:43,340
No, someone called from this harbor

373
00:22:43,340 --> 00:22:45,180
Thanks to the first person who reported it.

374
00:22:46,020 --> 00:22:48,080
But who on earth was it?

375
00:22:53,220 --> 00:22:54,200
That was close, that was close.

376
00:22:54,200 --> 00:22:56,440
We nearly got caught by the Chief.

377
00:22:57,460 --> 00:22:59,680
Now, quickly, get us out of this locker -

378
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:01,180
What?

379
00:23:01,180 --> 00:23:03,120
Senior Lukan, what is it this time?

380
00:23:04,540 --> 00:23:06,860
Hey, hey, we have nothing to do with this!

381
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:12,380
Hey, where are you taking us?

382
00:23:16,740 --> 00:23:19,540
Where on earth did Ryo-chan go?

383
00:23:19,540 --> 00:23:22,360
It's been a week since then, hasn't it?

384
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:25,280
He's probably off goofing
around somewhere again.

385
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:27,960
It's nothing new.

386
00:23:27,960 --> 00:23:28,700
Haah.

387
00:23:29,760 --> 00:23:30,200
Yes, that's true.

388
00:23:31,260 --> 00:23:31,700
Wow.

389
00:23:32,880 --> 00:23:35,080
When will we be able to go home?

390
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:38,940
My instinct says we should
see a town with people soon.

391
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:40,440
It's hot.

392
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:43,380
I want to go home already.

393
00:23:43,380 --> 00:23:44,040
Don't cry.

394
00:23:44,040 --> 00:23:45,160
Almost there.

395
00:23:46,640 --> 00:23:49,640
Even if you find an empty locker,

396
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:52,620
never go inside it.

397
00:23:53,300 --> 00:23:54,680
If you do,

398
00:23:56,440 --> 00:23:59,700
you might end up in the same mess we did.

399
00:24:06,120 --> 00:24:08,300
I want this, I want that!

400
00:24:08,300 --> 00:24:10,020
We tricked the Chief into joining the show.

401
00:24:10,020 --> 00:24:12,380
The Kameari shopping
street human claw machine!

402
00:24:12,380 --> 00:24:14,360
But why is the guest the chief?

403
00:24:15,180 --> 00:24:17,360
Don't worry, as long as we hide our faces,
no one will recognize us.

404
00:24:18,200 --> 00:24:20,440
Next time: "Desire, the Human Claw Machine!"

405
00:24:20,440 --> 00:24:21,380
See you then!

406
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:44,040
Sweet, melting together,
and solving, and swiftly, and helping

407
00:24:44,040 --> 00:24:55,700
decided, and inspired, and bouncing,
and gathering, and acting, and flying off

408
00:24:56,600 --> 00:25:00,380
Above all, an amazing power

409
00:25:00,380 --> 00:25:06,440
Gather everyone, if you come here

410
00:25:07,220 --> 00:25:12,680
Like a dream, the final energy

411
00:25:13,780 --> 00:25:17,140
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday

412
00:25:17,140 --> 00:25:20,040
Painting the universe,
if we stand on the ground

413
00:25:20,040 --> 00:25:23,840
Kameari's star spun around and drew a circle

414
00:25:25,940 --> 00:25:27,480
This should be fine, right

415
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:29,020
No way it's fine!

416
00:25:42,400 --> 00:25:43,800
Thank you for watching.

